  "prediction": "**Dry Ice Bomb Incident at Disneyland**\n\nA 22-year-old Disneyland employee, Christian Barnes, has been arrested in connection with the detonation of a dry ice bomb in the park's Toontown area. The explosion occurred on Tuesday evening, forcing the evacuation of the area for two hours. Fortunately, no one was injured in the incident.\n\nAccording to Anaheim police, Barnes, who worked as an outdoor vendor, placed dry ice in a plastic bottle that was left in a trash can in Toontown. The mixture exploded around 5:30 p.m., causing brief chaos in the popular area with young children.\n\nBarnes was booked on suspicion of possession of a destructive device and is being held in lieu of bail of $1 million. He is cooperating with investigators and has indicated that the incident was isolated with unanticipated impacts.\n\nDisneyland officials have released a statement saying they are working closely with local authorities to investigate the incident. The park's Toontown area, designed to resemble an old-fashioned cartoon, was briefly evacuated, but the explosion caused no significant damage.\n\nThe incident does not appear to be connected to similar dry-ice explosions in Anaheim in recent months, according to Anaheim police Sgt. Bob Dunn.\n\nThe incident has raised concerns about safety at the park, with one visitor commenting, \"You wouldn't expect situations like that coming to a place like this. That is crazy, that's wild.\"\n\nThe investigation into the incident is ongoing, and Barnes is being held on bail pending further investigation.\n\n**Other News**\n\n* A probe has been launched into the torture death of a Palmdale boy.\n* Two witnesses have disputed Justin Bieber's story about his Ferrari.\n* Cops who took a car on a joyride to Vegas have blamed a \"momentary\" lapse.",
